\description{
\code{mighty_codelists()} creates an S7 object for storing codelist metadata.
The class represents the contents of \verb{_codelists.yml} as a list of codelist
entries. Each codelist is referenced from column metadata via its \code{id}
(the \code{codelist} field of a column).

A codelist can contain the following operation groups:
\itemize{
\item \code{values}: values of a sponsor-defined (non-standard) codelist,
\item \code{subset}: values kept from a standard controlled terminology codelist,
\item \code{restore}: SDTM controlled terminology values included in the ADaM
codelist even when they are not used in the SDTM define.xml,
\item \code{extend}: values added to an extensible codelist.
}

\code{values} is meant for codelists that are not part of standard controlled
terminology, while \code{subset}, \code{restore} and \code{extend} modify a standard
codelist retrieved from an external source.

The object is validated on creation and when \code{validate()} is called.
Validation includes:
\itemize{
\item schema compliance with \code{inst/schema/codelists.json},
\item uniqueness of codelist identifiers (\code{id}),
\item uniqueness of \code{code} within a codelist across all operation groups,
\item \code{values} being mutually exclusive with \code{subset} and \code{restore},
\item consistent use of \code{decode} within an operation group (all or none).
}

When part of a \code{\link[=mighty_study]{mighty_study()}}, every codelist must also be referenced
by at least one column in the domain metadata.
}
\details{
Functions to list, select, define, remove, and update codelists and their
values in your \code{mighty_codelists()} object (or through
\code{mighty_study@codelists}).

Codelist level:
\itemize{
\item \code{define_codelist()} adds a new sponsor-defined codelist with \code{values}.
\item \code{remove_codelist()} removes codelist(s) and all their contents.
\item \code{update_codelist()} updates \code{label}, \code{description} and \code{datatype}.
\item \code{select_codelist()} returns a single codelist entry as a list.
}

Value level:
\itemize{
\item \code{define_codelist_values()} adds \code{values} to an existing codelist.
\item \code{extend_codelist_values()}, \code{restore_codelist_values()} and
\code{subset_codelist_values()} add \code{extend}, \code{restore} and \code{subset} entries,
creating the codelist if it does not exist.
\item \code{remove_codelist_value()} removes value(s) from whichever operation group
they belong to. Empty groups are dropped, and a codelist left without any
values is removed.
\item \code{move_codelist_value()} moves a value within its operation group.
\item \code{update_codelist_value()} updates the decode of a \code{values} or \code{extend}
entry.
}

When working on a \code{mighty_study()}, every codelist must be referenced by a
column (\code{codelist} field), so add the column reference before defining the
codelist.
}
